ELF symbol table: `sh_size / sizeof(Elf_Sym)` gives the number of entries. The first entry (index 0) is always STN_UNDEF with st_name=0. So the loop from i=0 includes it. But...

Wait, let me re-check. In the ELF spec, the symbol table does include entry 0. And `sh_size / sizeof(Elf_Sym)` counts ALL entries including entry 0. So the loop `for (i = 0; i < num; i++)` WOULD process entry 0.

But this must be working on other platforms. Let me check more carefully...

Actually, let me check if `libelf_findsymbol` has a check that I missed. Looking at the code again:

```c
for (i = 0; i < num; i++)
{
    ret = libelf_readsym(loadinfo, i, sym, ...);
    if (ret)
    {
        berr("ERROR: Failed to read symbol entry\n");
        return ret;
    }

    ret = libelf_symname(loadinfo, sym, ...);
    if (ret < 0 && ret != -ESRCH)
