// libelf_findsymbol is ONLY called if bind succeeds
```

So if libelf_bind fails (which it SHOULD with exports=NULL for an ET_REL with SHN_UNDEF symbols), `libelf_findsymbol` is never reached. The error goes to `errout_with_load` which cleans up.

But wait, what if the init ELF has NO external symbol references? What if all symbols are defined internally? Then `libelf_bind` would succeed (no SHN_UNDEF symbols to resolve), and `libelf_findsymbol` would be called. Then the crash would happen in `libelf_findsymbol` with the unnamed symbol 0.

But this would crash on ALL platforms, not just SG2000. Unless other platforms have `libelf_allocbuffer` called from a different code path before `libelf_findsymbol`.

